    fuentes: [{ title: "Jump starting a car", body: "To jump start a car, connect the red cable to the positive terminal of the dead battery first. Do not connect the black cable to the negative terminal of the dead battery. Connect the black cable to a metal part of the engine, away from the battery. A healthy battery holds 12 volts. Wait 5 minutes before trying to start the car. Roadside assistance answers on 800-555-0162. This guide was reviewed on November 2, 2023." }],
    respuesta: "Connect the red cable to the positive terminal of the dead battery first, and wait five minutes before trying to start the car.",
