    fuentes: [{ title: "Main water shutoff", body: "The main water shutoff valve is usually near the water meter or where the pipe enters the house. Turn the valve clockwise to close it and stop the water flow. Do not use a metal wrench on a plastic valve. A leaking tap can waste 15 liters of water a day. The meter is read every 30 days by the water company. If a pipe bursts, call a plumber at 800-555-0128; for a major flood call 911. This guide was reviewed on January 27, 2024." }, { title: "Reservoirs", body: "The reservoir north of the town holds water for 30 villages in the surrounding valley and fills during the winter rains." }, { title: "Photosynthesis", body: "Photosynthesis is a process used by plants and other organisms to convert light energy into chemical energy, which is later released to fuel the organism's activities. In most cases, oxygen is released as a waste product." }],
