    fuentes: [{ title: "Main water shutoff", body: "The main water shutoff valve is usually near the water meter or where the pipe enters the house. Turn the valve clockwise to close it and stop the water flow. Do not use a metal wrench on a plastic valve. A leaking tap can waste 15 liters of water a day. The meter is read every 30 days by the water company. If a pipe bursts, call a plumber at 800-555-0128; for a major flood call 911. This guide was reviewed on January 27, 2024." }],
    respuesta: "1. Turn the valve clockwise to close it and stop the water flow. 2. Open the taps to drain the pipes. 3. Hit the valve with a shoe until it bends shut.",
